From 8b46bd648737d9fcd6abd7f866bb2677e78af8d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:42:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/dashdec: clear pending segment restart when seeking

Probing a small fragment can reach EOF and set is_restart_needed before a
seek. dash_seek selects a new segment but leaves this flag set, so
read_data does not advance cur_seq_no at the next EOF. The selected
segment is then opened a second time.

Clear the pending restart along with the other segment read state before
reopening the component. Do this before probing the new segment, which
may legitimately set the flag again.

Add generated MP2 DASH tests comparing seek-to-zero and sequential packet
checksums and timestamps. The seek test emits 14 duplicate packets without
the reset; both tests produce the same 42 packets with it.

Fixes #25247

Assisted-by: Fairy
(cherry picked from commit 8b46bd648737d9fcd6abd7f866bb2677e78af8d1)

Hades: the FATE test of this commit (tests/fate/dashenc.mak,
tests/ref/fate/dash-seek-zero) is left out: the entries around it in
9.0.2's tests/fate/dashenc.mak differ from master's. The change to
dashdec.c is upstream's.
---
 libavformat/dashdec.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/libavformat/dashdec.c b/libavformat/dashdec.c
index 1969cc034f78..eaf7c2afb476 100644
--- a/libavformat/dashdec.c
+++ b/libavformat/dashdec.c
@@ -2517,6 +2517,7 @@ set_seq_num:
     pls->cur_timestamp = 0;
     pls->cur_seg_offset = 0;
     pls->init_sec_buf_read_offset = 0;
+    pls->is_restart_needed = 0;
     ret = dry_run ? 0 : reopen_demux_for_component(s, pls);
 
     return ret;
